                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.29064/2611.29064v1/method_v2.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:From three networks to one shared transformer.(a)Separate: the standard latent-diffusion pipeline trains an encoderEθE_{\\theta}, a generatorGψG_{\\psi}, and a decoderDϕD_{\\phi}.(b)UNITE shares one backbone between encoding and generation; the\nencoding pass appends𝒩⁡(0,I)\\mathcal{N}(0,I)readout tokens to the image patches\nand takes the latentzzfrom their outputs, but a standalone decoderDϕD_{\\phi}remains.(c)UNITE++ folds decoding into the same backbone as a third mode,\nselected by a mode token, but keeps readout tokens for encoding (latent\nreadouts) and decoding (pixel readouts).(d)UNIFIED (ours) removes all readout tokens: every pass maps a\nsame-length, position-aligned sequence (imagexx, noisy latentztz_{t}, or\nlatentzz) after a mode token at position00, and encodes clean images attenc=1t_{\\mathrm{enc}}=1rather than00. Bottom right: each model’s\nencoding and decoding timesteps.",
